.TH AUDIT2FIVEW 1 "2026-11-02" "audit2fivew 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
audit2fivew \- Terminal UI for SELinux AVC denial troubleshooting
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B audit2fivew
[\fB\-log\fR \fIpath\fR]
[\fB\-db\fR \fIpath\fR]
[\fB\-version\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBaudit2fivew\fR is a non-destructive, fully-offline Terminal User Interface
(TUI) utility designed for inspecting, troubleshooting, and resolving SELinux
Access Vector Cache (AVC) denials.
.PP
It ingests denial events from the Linux audit daemon log
(\fI/var/log/audit/audit.log\fR) and augments them via \fBausearch\fR(8).
Denials are parsed, deduplicated, and persisted in a local SQLite database
for historical analysis across log rotations.
.PP
The interactive interface presents a split master-detail view organized around
the \(lqFive Ws\(rq framework, explaining in plain terms:
.TP
\(bu
\fBWhen\fR \(em The exact timestamp of the denial.
.TP
\(bu
\fBWho\fR \(em Source SELinux security context, executable name (\fIcomm\fR),
and Process ID (\fIPID\fR).
.TP
\(bu
\fBWhere\fR \(em Target SELinux security context and path or device name.
.TP
\(bu
\fBWhat\fR \(em Target security class (e.g. \fIfile\fR, \fIsocket\fR) and
denied permissions.
.TP
\(bu
\fBWay to Fix\fR \(em Synthesized Type Enforcement (\fI.te\fR) policy rules
and the exact commands required to build and load a custom policy module
using \fBcheckmodule\fR(8) and \fBsemodule\fR(8).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-log \ path
Path to the SELinux audit log file.
Default: \fI/var/log/audit/audit.log\fR
.TP
.BI \-db \ path
Path to the SQLite database used for persisting and tracking denial history.
Default: \fI~/.local/share/audit2fivew/denials.db\fR
.TP
.B \-version
Display version information and exit.
.SH INTERACTIVE CONTROLS
While in the interactive TUI, the following keybindings are available:
.SS Global
.TP
.B q\fR, \fBCtrl+c
Quit \fBaudit2fivew\fR.
.TP
.B Tab
Switch focus between the denial list pane and the detail inspection pane.
.TP
.B /
Enter filter mode. Begin typing to filter the denial list by source type,
target type, or permission.
.TP
.B Esc
Exit filter mode, or clear the active filter string if not typing.
.TP
.B r
Trigger an immediate refresh to re-read new denials from the audit log
and \fBausearch\fR(8).
.SS List Pane (Left)
.TP
.B Up\fR, \fBk
Move the selection cursor up.
.TP
.B Down\fR, \fBj
Move the selection cursor down.
.SS Detail Pane (Right)
.TP
.B Up\fR, \fBk
Scroll the detail viewport up.
.TP
.B Down\fR, \fBj
Scroll the detail viewport down.
.TP
.B g
Scroll to the top of the detail viewport.
.TP
.B G
Scroll to the bottom of the detail viewport.
.TP
.B Mouse Wheel
Scroll the detail pane content.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/log/audit/audit.log
Default system audit log containing raw SELinux AVC messages. Reading this
file typically requires superuser (\fBroot\fR) privileges or membership in
the \fIaudit\fR group.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/audit2fivew/denials.db
SQLite database storing deduplicated historical denials and metadata.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Successful completion.
.TP
.B 1
Initialization failure (e.g., unable to open or create SQLite database
directory, or terminal UI runtime error).
.SH NOTES
\fBaudit2fivew\fR is strictly non-destructive. It reads audit logs and writes
only to its local user database. It never modifies active SELinux policy
or system audit configuration. To apply generated remediation rules, review
the suggested commands in the \(lqWay to Fix\(rq section and execute them
manually with administrative privileges.
